{{further|2026 Japan Open Tennis Championships}}

[[Carlos Alcaraz]] is the defending champion.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/tennis/articles/c89d5n3wz2no|title=Alcaraz wins eighth title of season in Tokyo|publisher=BBC Sport|accessdate=30 September 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.atptour.com/en/news/alcaraz-fritz-tokyo-2025-final|title= Alcaraz exacts quick Fritz revenge, captures Tokyo title on debut |date= 30 September 2025|website=ATPTour}}</ref>

This tournament marked the final professional appearance of [[2014 US Open – Men's singles|2014 US Open]] finalist, [[Tennis at the 2016 Summer Olympics – Men's singles|2016 Olympic bronze medalist]], and former world No. 4 [[Kei Nishikori]].<ref>{{cite web |author1=Kyodo News |title=Tennis: Nishikori vows to give all at career-ending Japan Open |url=https://english.kyodonews.net/articles/-/86329 |website=Japan Wire by Kyodo News |access-date=28 September 2026 |date=25 September 2026}}</ref> He lost in the first round to [[Frances Tiafoe]].<ref> {{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/tennis/articles/cwe8e81n3egeo|title='I kept fighting right to the end' - emotional Nishikori retires |date=1 October 2026}}</ref>

